topics.description:
The **Django Template Language (DTL)** keeps logic simple on purpose; heavy computation belongs in views and models.

### Syntax
- Variables: `{{ post.title }}` (auto-escaped; dotted lookups try dict key, attribute, then index).
- Tags: `{% if %}`, `{% for %}`, `{% url %}`, `{% include %}`, `{% block %}`, `{% extends %}`, `{% csrf_token %}`, `{% load static %}`.
- Filters: `{{ text|truncatewords:20 }}`, `|date:"d M Y"`, `|default:"-"`, `|length`, `|safe`.
- Comments: `{# note #}`.

### Inheritance
```html
{# base.html #}
<title>{% block title %}Site{% endblock %}</title>
{% block content %}{% endblock %}

{# list.html #}
{% extends "base.html" %}
{% block content %}
  {% for post in posts %}
    <h2><a href="{{ post.get_absolute_url }}">{{ post.title }}</a></h2>
  {% empty %}
    <p>No posts yet.</p>
  {% endfor %}
{% endblock %}
```

### Static files
`{% load static %}` then `<link rel="stylesheet" href="{% static 'css/site.css' %}">`.

### Forms
`<form method="post">{% csrf_token %}{{ form.as_p }}</form>` for quick pages; render fields individually for custom design.

### Custom tags and filters
Create `templatetags/` in an app and register with `@register.filter` or `@register.simple_tag`.

### Alternatives
Django can also use **Jinja2**; many modern projects pair Django with React/Vue and expose APIs through DRF instead.

examples.code:
{# templates/base.html #}
{% load static %}
<!doctype html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>{% block title %}My Blog{% endblock %}</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{% static 'css/site.css' %}">
</head>
<body>
  <header>
    {% if user.is_authenticated %}
      Hi {{ user.username }} | <a href="{% url 'logout' %}">Logout</a>
    {% else %}
      <a href="{% url 'login' %}">Login</a>
    {% endif %}
  </header>
  {% if messages %}
    {% for m in messages %}<p class="{{ m.tags }}">{{ m }}</p>{% endfor %}
  {% endif %}
  {% block content %}{% endblock %}
</body>
</html>

{# blog/templates/blog/list.html #}
{% extends "base.html" %}
{% block title %}Posts{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
  {% for post in posts %}
    <article>
      <h2><a href="{% url 'blog:detail' slug=post.slug %}">{{ post.title }}</a></h2>
      <small>{{ post.created_at|date:"d M Y" }} by {{ post.author }}</small>
      <p>{{ post.body|truncatewords:30 }}</p>
    </article>
  {% empty %}
    <p>No posts yet.</p>
  {% endfor %}
{% endblock %}

# forms.py
from django import forms
from .models import Post

class ContactForm(forms.Form):
    name = forms.CharField(max_length=80)
    email = forms.EmailField()
    message = forms.CharField(widget=forms.Textarea, min_length=10)

    def clean_name(self):
        name = self.cleaned_data["name"].strip()
        if name.lower() == "admin":
            raise forms.ValidationError("Choose a different name")
        return name

class PostForm(forms.ModelForm):
    class Meta:
        model = Post
        fields = ["title", "slug", "category", "body"]
        widgets = {"body": forms.Textarea(attrs={"rows": 8, "class": "input"})}

# views.py
from django.contrib import messages
from django.shortcuts import render, redirect

def contact(request):
    form = ContactForm(request.POST or None)
    if request.method == "POST" and form.is_valid():
        data = form.cleaned_data
        # send_mail(...)
        messages.success(request, f"Thanks {data['name']}!")
        return redirect("contact")
    return render(request, "contact.html", {"form": form})

from django.contrib import admin
from .models import Post, Comment

class CommentInline(admin.TabularInline):
    model = Comment
    extra = 0

@admin.register(Post)
class PostAdmin(admin.ModelAdmin):
    list_display = ("title", "author", "status", "created_at", "comment_count")
    list_filter = ("status", "created_at")
    search_fields = ("title", "author__username")
    prepopulated_fields = {"slug": ("title",)}
    inlines = [CommentInline]
    list_select_related = ("author",)

    @admin.display(description="Comments")
    def comment_count(self, obj):
        return obj.comments.count()

# accounts/views.py
from django.contrib.auth import login, get_user_model
from django.contrib.auth.decorators import login_required, permission_required
from django.contrib.auth.forms import UserCreationForm
from django.shortcuts import render, redirect

User = get_user_model()

def signup(request):
    form = UserCreationForm(request.POST or None)
    if form.is_valid():
        user = form.save()          # password is hashed
        login(request, user)
        return redirect("dashboard")
    return render(request, "registration/signup.html", {"form": form})

@login_required
def dashboard(request):
    return render(request, "dashboard.html", {"posts": request.user.posts.all()})

